{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC5 MEASUREMENT CAMPAIGN -- peak RSS per gate run, ten samples collected in real time tonight.\n\nEvery GATE_PEAK_RSS marker emitted during this session's gate runs, from the marker that landed in\nchange 2589. These are real production-shaped runs against this store, not a synthetic benchmark:\n\n  gate               ticket   peak_rss_bytes   MB     elapsed_ms\n  plan_review        7dfa     748,437,504      713.8   221,616\n  verify_completion  7dfa     461,766,656      440.4    80,910\n  verify_completion  9a17     438,730,752      418.4    ~80,000\n  verify_completion  c379     457,752,576      436.5    67,444\n  verify_completion  740d     440,221,696      419.8    83,913\n  verify_completion  477b     438,534,144      418.2    74,926\n  verify_completion  09da     453,132,288      432.1   112,420\n  verify_completion  860b     438,714,368      418.4   100,917\n  verify_completion  aa40     455,049,216      434.0   119,061\n  verify_completion  1035     439,910,400      419.5    97,633\n\nWHAT THIS SETTLES:\n - PLAN-REVIEW peak is ~714 MB (single sample; the epic's sizing used ~739 MB, so that estimate was\n   sound and slightly conservative).\n - COMPLETION-VERIFIER peak is remarkably TIGHT: nine samples spanning 418.2-440.4 MB, mean ~430 MB,\n   spread under 6%. That is a much more predictable figure than expected, and it is the one to plan\n   against for the close gate.\n - The two gates are NOT interchangeable for sizing: plan-review peaks ~1.66x the completion\n   verifier. A single 'gate RSS' number would overstate one and understate the other.\n - peak_delta_bytes was 0 on most verify_completion runs and 521,961,472 on the plan_review run,\n   i.e. plan-review is where the allocation actually happens; the close gate largely runs inside\n   memory the process already had.\n\nCROSS-CHECK AGAINST S6, which shipped on this basis: S6's default cap of 4 was derived as\n4 x ~748 MB ~= 2.99 GB against ~3 GiB of headroom. These ten samples support that arithmetic for\nplan_review and suggest it is CONSERVATIVE for completion-verifier, where four concurrent runs would\nbe ~1.72 GB rather than ~2.99 GB. So the cap is safe, and if it ever needs raising, doing so per-gate\nrather than globally is the option the data supports.\n\nWHAT IS STILL MISSING for AC5 as written, stated plainly rather than glossed:\n - STEADY-STATE RSS PER CONTAINER: not collected here. That needs the container_memory_rss_bytes\n   series from observability.sh section 2d on the box, which is AC4's post-deploy half.\n - HOW RSS SCALES WITH TICKET SIZE: not collected. Every sample above is one store and a range of\n   ticket sizes I did not control or record, so I cannot honestly attribute the 418-440 MB spread to\n   ticket size rather than to noise. Establishing that needs a deliberate campaign across known\n   description/comment sizes, not opportunistic collection.\n\nSo AC5 is PARTIALLY satisfied: the peak-RSS-per-gate-run term is now measured with ten samples, and\nthe other two terms remain open. Not ticking it."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788531443132967001,"uuid":"7698fc30-9807-4d03-890a-de7785908afb"}